<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chitpavan Brahmins</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chitpavan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> are a Brahmin community from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Their influence grew in the 18th century, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a>, the hereditary chief ministers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state, came from the community. Chitpavan families such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patwardhan">Patwardhans</a> became generals and were rewarded with lands in the southern Maratha country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chitpavan-brahmins.jpg" alt="Chitpavan Brahmins" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Soorya Hebbar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%AC%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%A1%E0%A4%A3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
